-# auth_token_service
+# Auth token service
+
+An in-memory Python authentication service with registration and signed-token login. User records are not persisted between process restarts; this intentionally satisfies the no-external-database constraint.
+
+## Run
+
+Requires Python 3.10+ and `pytest` for the test suite.
+
+```bash
+export AUTH_TOKEN_SECRET='replace-with-a-long-random-secret'
+python -m app
+```
+
+The service listens on `http://127.0.0.1:8000`.
+
+```bash
+curl -X POST http://127.0.0.1:8000/register -H 'Content-Type: application/json' -d '{"username":"ada","password":"secret"}'
+curl -X POST http://127.0.0.1:8000/login -H 'Content-Type: application/json' -d '{"username":"ada","password":"secret"}'
+```
+
+Only `POST /register` and `POST /login` are implemented. There is deliberately no user-deletion endpoint.
+
+## Test
+
+```bash
+python -m pytest
+```
+
+## Requirement evidence
+
+- **REQ-001:** `test_req_001_register_stores_user_without_plaintext_password` verifies registration stores a user record.
+- **REQ-002:** `test_req_002_login_returns_a_non_empty_token_string` verifies successful login returns a token string.
